module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.function_parameter_call_emitted_as_a_same_named_top_level_fn

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data function_parameter_call_emitted_as_a_same_named_top_level_fn: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "function_parameter_call_emitted_as_a_same_named_top_level_fn" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a call through a function-typed PARAMETER whose name matches a top-level fn declared in another module is emitted by the Rust emitter as a call to that top-level fn. The local binding loses to the module-level name, even though the interpreter and the checker bind the parameter correctly.",

    "RECEIPT 2026-10-12, gunbc#13782: v2.compiler.parse parse_module_authored took `normalize: fn(String) -> String`. The emitted crate called v2.compiler.normalize normalize, a later stage, and the crate plan refused it as EmitterReverseEdge. The claims passed under the interpreter. The parameter was renamed `annotation_text`, which avoids the refusal and does not repair the emitter.",

    "RECEIPT 2026-10-31, snappy-carp-24 (verification of gunb-ai/gunbc#15493): the mis-bound caller is STD itself now. Compiling dag/test/claim/compute/work_request_witness.dag for rust at d217e9c0853b (main 33b8d5a8729f merged; local binary b13faa6dc70, freshness unproven -- an srv1 run at the same head is queued to confirm) emitted with 0 hard diagnostics and was refused at workspace realization: 'EMITTED-WORKSPACE REFUSAL cause=WorkspaceNotRealized -- PlanRefused: EmitterReverseEdge std_algebra -> test_claim_compute_work_request_witness'. The pair names itself: std.algebra list_sort_by_key takes `key: fn(T) -> K` and calls key(item) at dag/std/algebra.dag:1431, while the witness declares a top-level fn key at dag/test/claim/compute/work_request_witness.dag:198. The emitted std_algebra calls the claim file's key, so the emitted std crate depends on a test crate and the edge closes a cycle the source does not have. Same mechanism as the parse_module_authored receipt, wider reach: std on the caller side, a claim file on the target side.",

    "WHAT THE REFUSAL COSTS THE READER, measured while tracing this pair: gunbc.emitted_crate_workspace emitted_workspace_edge_refusal_message (dag/gunbc/emitted_crate_workspace.dag:468) renders the arm as 'EmitterReverseEdge <from> -> <to>' and discards the provenance gunbc.crate_partition attached when minting it (dag/gunbc/crate_partition.dag:233), although the comment above the formatter says 'each arm names its members, so the line says which module or edge to look at'. The pair alone does not say which call produced the edge, so it had to be re-derived by hand from the two sites quoted above. Named here, not fixed here: rendering edge.provenance in that one line is that module's change, not this row's.",

    "HARM: the refusal in the receipt is INCIDENTAL. It fired only because the mis-bound target sat in a later stage, which forms a reverse edge. Where the same-named fn is reachable without a cycle, and its signature fits, the emitted program calls the wrong function silently. That is below the ladder.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the wrong binding appears only in emission, never in interpretation, so no claim run observes it. The control that would discriminate is an emitted-and-executed program whose parameter shadows a reachable top-level fn of the same signature, asserting that the parameter's value is the one called.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent) in general; mechanically refused only by accident when the mis-bound target forms a reverse crate edge. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- name resolution is decidable and the emitter must consume the resolved binding the checker already computed rather than re-resolving by spelling. NEXT TRIGGER: the Rust emitter reads each call's callee from the resolved binding of its occurrence (local parameter before module scope), plus an emitted-and-executed shadowing control enrolled under the required gate."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.parse", decl_name: "parse_module_authored", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
